          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "したがう (shitagau) is a native Japanese word (wago), inherited rather than borrowed from Chinese, and its older origin is not settled. Its kanji was attached to it later as a kun'yomi, a native reading given to a Chinese character (JMdict, KANJIDIC2)."
